menu "Fan Controller Configuration"

    config FAN_WIFI_SSID
        string "WiFi SSID"
        default ""
        help
            SSID of the WLAN to join for the HTTP status page. Leave empty
            to run without WiFi (USB serial control is unaffected).
            Set this in sdkconfig.secrets, not in sdkconfig.defaults.

    config FAN_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "WiFi password"
        default ""
        help
            WPA2 passphrase. Empty means an open network.
            Set this in sdkconfig.secrets, not in sdkconfig.defaults.

    config FAN_HOSTNAME
        string "Hostname (mDNS)"
        default "fan-controller"
        help
            The device is reachable at http://<hostname>.local when WiFi
            is connected.

    config FAN_FAILSAFE_TIMEOUT_S
        int "Failsafe timeout (seconds)"
        range 5 600
        default 30
        help
            If no PWM command arrives over USB serial for this long, the fan
            is forced to 100% until the host resumes sending them. Only PWM
            counts: STATUS, VER and PING deliberately do not reset the timer,
            because they prove the link is alive without proving the host is
            still controlling the fan. fan-controllerd requires its poll
            interval plus its 3 s serial exchange budget to be at most half of
            this value. STATUS reports the value as FAILSAFE_TIMEOUT, so the
            daemon checks its own setting against it when it connects.

    config FAN_BOOT_DUTY_PERCENT
        int "Fan duty at boot (%)"
        range 50 100
        default 100
        help
            Duty applied from power-up until the first PWM command from the
            host, and after every reboot. The range starts at 50% because the
            drives are unprotected for the whole failsafe timeout at this duty:
            0 would have meant no airflow at all for up to 600 s on every boot.

endmenu
